{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792309738,"nonce":"n3MCUm7ahRKj0V6vAakZPgOIbao=","title":"Code editor scroll costs 4-8 ms of flush a step, whatever the step","message":"User report: the code editor lags while scrolling, worst as a flick decelerates. scripts/scroll-bench.sh (tests/ScrollBench.hx) times a 4800-line file offscreen. A scroll step costs 5-6 ms of LayoutTree.flush at 52, 11, 2.4 and 0.2 px alike, and nothing at 0 px; a plain scroll view of 1000 rows costs nothing, so the cost is CodeEditor's. Cause: ashui.ui.For calls replaceChildren on every reconcile, even for an unchanged child list, and the cascade restyles all siblings (NativeCascade.restyle 23% of samples). A 13-line patch to For (skip an unchanged replaceChildren) takes the 0.2 px step to 0.1 ms flush and the whole frame from 14.8 to 5.1 ms, validated in RayDE's .deps clone and reverted. Rows entering the window still cost 8-13 ms a frame at 11-52 px steps (about 30 elements a row restyled): pool the row elements and compute the window as row indices. Sent to ashui (ashui-8c); blinc_ts's recent scroll work (text and primitive culling, 74c55a5 and 16e2bc9) is already in the pinned blinc_abi, and its frame-in-flight change targets backdrop blur, not this. Re-run the bench after each ashui pin.","files":null}]}